WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.140
Two findings both end with a mouse not breathing.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.440
Are they the same line, used twice?

3
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:11.233
Start with the opposite results.

4
00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:16.413
Light on P2ry1 afferents suppressed breathing in anaesthetized mice.

5
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:21.707
Light on Npy2r afferents produced rapid shallow breathing.

6
00:00:22.407 --> 00:00:24.227
Opposite outputs, in the same nerve.

7
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.390
This is sufficiency.

8
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:34.370
It says what each population can do when driven, not what drives it in life.

9
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.080
Nerve recordings added an independent check.

10
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.200
One population was mostly fast, the other mostly slow.

11
00:00:43.233 --> 00:00:46.053
A fibres are myelinated and conduct quickly.

12
00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.533
C fibres are unmyelinated and conduct slowly.

13
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:54.033
Conduction speed was measured apart from the breathing assay.

14
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.733
Most of one population conducted fast, most of the other slow.

15
00:00:59.553 --> 00:01:03.193
That is a physiological difference, not proof of complete separation.

16
00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:10.477
Now the two routes to one output.

17
00:01:11.557 --> 00:01:15.937
First, inflation. When the lungs fill, further inspiration is cut short.

18
00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:21.687
This is the Hering-Breuer inflation reflex, described more than a century ago.

19
00:01:22.587 --> 00:01:24.507
Cut both vagi and the reflex goes.

20
00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.727
Second, protection.

21
00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:32.407
Water or acid at the larynx triggers protective reflexes that keep the airway clear.

22
00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:39.210
Driving P2ry1 afferents with light recruited the whole program, not apnoea alone.

23
00:01:42.283 --> 00:01:46.523
Ablating those cells impaired swallowing to laryngeal water and acid.

24
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:49.103
That is necessity, in that assay.

25
00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:55.053
So these cells can recruit airway defence, and one tested piece of it needs them.

26
00:01:57.233 --> 00:02:01.293
If they were also the lung's stretch detector, what would inflation imaging show?

27
00:02:07.317 --> 00:02:12.497
If one population did both jobs, the inflation responders should sit inside the

28
00:02:12.497 --> 00:02:13.497
labelled set.

29
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:19.250
They did not. Most stretch-responsive neurons were PIEZO2-positive and

30
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.870
P2RY1-negative.

31
00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:30.323
That imaging was done with central connections severed, under isoflurane, with the

32
00:02:30.323 --> 00:02:32.083
airway inflated in the living animal.

33
00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:36.633
So two populations, two challenges, one shared output.

34
00:02:37.453 --> 00:02:38.813
The table separates them.

35
00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.247
The takeaway is general.

36
00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:57.847
An output alone does not identify which pathway produced it.

37
00:02:58.547 --> 00:03:00.347
Measure stimulus and output separately.
